<title>JAPAN: M'bishi Corp to buy into Chinese supermarket firm.</title>
<headline>M'bishi Corp to buy into Chinese supermarket firm.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Corp said on Monday that it had agreed with Shanghai Lian Hua Supermarket Co Ltd to buy a partial stake in the state-owned Chinese supermarket chain.</p>
<p>Mitsubishi will purchase new shares to be issued by the Chinese firm. Mitsubishi will own 15 percent of the firm's 2.5 billion yen capital, a Mitsubishi spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Chinese firm currently operates 108 stores located mainly in Shanghai, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman said that the move is partly aimed at researching consumption patterns in China.</p>
</text>
